{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"motor-drivers","name":"Motor drivers and movers","version":"1.0.1","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"More ways to drive and move things: the TB6612FNG (two small motors, efficient) and BTS7960 (one big motor, 43 A) drivers, a vibration motor that really shakes what it's on, a push-pull solenoid, and a linear actuator.","category":"Motion","needsApp":"0.8.0","code":"// Motor drivers and movers. The drivers put out the motor's average voltage (a board's PWM duty times\r\n// their supply), which is what a motor's speed follows.\r\n\r\n/** a control pin's level as a share of the time it's HIGH (PWM), or 0 / 1 */\r\nconst duty = (io, pin) => {\r\n  const p = io.pwm(pin);\r\n  if (p && p.hz > 0) return Math.max(0, Math.min(1, p.duty));\r\n  return io.level(pin) === 1 ? 1 : 0;\r\n};\r\n\r\n// TB6612FNG: two H-bridges. IN1/IN2 pick the way (or brake / coast), PWM the speed, STBY wakes it.\r\nbench.device('tb6612', (part) => {\r\n  let vm = 0, logic = false, awake = false;\r\n  const ch = { A: 'stop', B: 'stop' };\r\n  const channel = (io, n, in1, in2, pwm, o1, o2) => {\r\n    const a = io.level(in1) === 1, b = io.level(in2) === 1, d = duty(io, pwm);\r\n    if (!logic || !awake || vm < 2.5) { io.release(o1); io.release(o2); ch[n] = 'off'; return; }\r\n    if (a && b) { io.drive(o1, 0, 2); io.drive(o2, 0, 2); ch[n] = 'brake'; return; }\r\n    if (!a && !b) { io.release(o1); io.release(o2); ch[n] = 'coast'; return; }\r\n    // (PWM LOW = short brake: the motor sees the average)\r\n    const v = vm * d;\r\n    io.drive(a ? o1 : o2, v, 2);\r\n    io.drive(a ? o2 : o1, 0, 2);\r\n    ch[n] = `${a ? 'forward' : 'back'} ${Math.round(d * 100)} %`;\r\n  };\r\n  return {\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      vm = io.supply('VM', 'GND');\r\n      logic = io.supply('VCC', 'GND') >= 2.7;\r\n      awake = io.level('STBY') === 1;\r\n      channel(io, 'A', 'AIN1', 'AIN2', 'PWMA', 'AO1', 'AO2');\r\n      channel(io, 'B', 'BIN1', 'BIN2', 'PWMB', 'BO1', 'BO2');\r\n      io.draw(logic ? 0.002 : 0);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      if (!logic) return ['no logic power (VCC)'];\r\n      if (!awake) return ['asleep: STBY must be HIGH'];\r\n      if (vm < 2.5) return ['no motor power (VM)'];\r\n      return [`motor A: ${ch.A}`, `motor B: ${ch.B}`, `VM ${vm.toFixed(1)} V`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n\r\n// BTS7960: two half bridges; RPWM drives M+ up, LPWM drives M- up, both enables must be HIGH.\r\nbench.device('bts7960', (part) => {\r\n  let vb = 0, state = 'off';\r\n  return {\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      vb = io.supply('B+', 'B-');\r\n      const logic = io.supply('VCC', 'GND') >= 3;\r\n      const en = io.level('R_EN') === 1 && io.level('L_EN') === 1;\r\n      if (!logic || !en || vb < 5.5) {\r\n        io.release('M+'); io.release('M-');\r\n        state = !logic ? 'no logic power (VCC)' : !en ? 'off: R_EN and L_EN must be HIGH' : 'no motor power (B+ / B-)';\r\n      } else {\r\n        const r = duty(io, 'RPWM'), l = duty(io, 'LPWM');\r\n        io.drive('M+', vb * r, 2);\r\n        io.drive('M-', vb * l, 2);\r\n        state = r && l ? `both sides on (${Math.round(r * 100)} % / ${Math.round(l * 100)} %): it brakes` : r ? `one way, ${Math.round(r * 100)} %` : l ? `the other way, ${Math.round(l * 100)} %` : 'stopped';\r\n      }\r\n      io.drive('R_IS', 0, 1);\r\n      io.drive('L_IS', 0, 1);\r\n      io.draw(logic ? 0.01 : 0);\r\n    },\r\n    status: () => [state, `${vb.toFixed(1)} V`],\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n\r\n// A vibration motor: its off-centre weight spins with the voltage it gets.\r\nbench.device('vibration', (part) => {\r\n  const w = part.motor('weight');\r\n  let v = 0;\r\n  return {\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      v = io.supply('+', '-');\r\n      if (Math.abs(v) < 0.4) w.limp();\r\n      else w.power(Math.sign(v), Math.abs(v));\r\n      io.draw(Math.abs(v) < 0.4 ? 0 : 0.08 * Math.min(1.5, Math.abs(v) / 3));\r\n    },\r\n    status: () => [Math.abs(v) < 0.4 ? 'off' : `buzzing (${v.toFixed(1)} V, ${Math.round(Math.abs(w.speed) / 6)} rpm)`],\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n\r\n// A push-pull solenoid: powered, the coil pulls the plunger in; off, the spring pushes it out.\r\nbench.device('solenoid', (part) => {\r\n  const plunger = part.motor('plunger');\r\n  let v = 0;\r\n  return {\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      v = Math.abs(io.supply('+', '-'));\r\n      if (v >= 3) plunger.to(-1.0, v);\r\n      else plunger.to(0, 3); // (the spring: weaker than the coil)\r\n      io.draw(v >= 3 ? v / 20 : 0); // (a 20 ohm coil)\r\n    },\r\n    status: () => [v >= 3 ? `pulled in (${v.toFixed(1)} V, ${(v / 20).toFixed(2)} A)` : 'out (spring)', `plunger at ${plunger.angle.toFixed(2)} cm`],\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n\r\n// A linear actuator: a DC motor on a screw; it stops at the ends of its travel by itself.\r\nbench.device('actuator', (part) => {\r\n  const rod = part.motor('rod');\r\n  let v = 0, atEnd = false;\r\n  return {\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      v = io.supply('M+', 'M-');\r\n      atEnd = (v > 0 && rod.angle >= 9.95) || (v < 0 && rod.angle <= 0.05);\r\n      if (Math.abs(v) < 0.5 || atEnd) rod.power(0, 12);\r\n      else rod.power(Math.sign(v), Math.abs(v));\r\n      io.draw(Math.abs(v) < 0.5 || atEnd ? 0 : 1.2 * Math.min(1.5, Math.abs(v) / 12));\r\n    },\r\n    status: () => [Math.abs(v) < 0.5 ? 'stopped' : atEnd ? `at its ${v > 0 ? 'outer' : 'inner'} end (its end switch stopped it)` : v > 0 ? 'pushing out' : 'pulling in', `rod out ${rod.angle.toFixed(1)} cm of 10`],\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n","parts":[{"id":"tb6612","name":"Motor driver (TB6612FNG, 2 channels)","description":"Drives two DC motors (up to 1.2 A each) from VM (4.5-13.5 V), controlled by a board: AIN1 / AIN2 set the way motor A turns (HIGH/LOW forward, LOW/HIGH back, both HIGH brake, both LOW coast), PWMA its speed (analogWrite), the same for B. STBY must be HIGH or nothing moves. VCC is the logic supply (2.7-5.5 V).","swatch":"#c0392b","mass":3,"shape":[{"box":[2,0.16,2],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#b0302a"},{"box":[0.9,0.12,0.9],"at":[0,0.22,0],"color":"#151618","collide":false}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["VM","VCC","GND","AO1","AO2","BO2","BO1","GND2"],"at":[-0.889,0.16,0.85],"dir":"x","kinds":{"VM":"vin","VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd","GND2":"gnd","AO1":"motor","AO2":"motor","BO1":"motor","BO2":"motor"},"extra":{"VM":{"label":"VM (motor power 4.5-13.5 V)","vmin":2.5,"vmax":15},"VCC":{"label":"VCC (logic 2.7-5.5 V)","vmin":2.7,"vmax":5.5}}},{"ids":["PWMA","AIN2","AIN1","STBY","BIN1","BIN2","PWMB","GND3"],"at":[-0.889,0.16,-0.85],"dir":"x","kinds":{"PWMA":"in","AIN2":"in","AIN1":"in","STBY":"in","BIN1":"in","BIN2":"in","PWMB":"in","GND3":"gnd"}}],"shorts":[["GND","GND2"],["GND","GND3"]],"device":"tb6612"},{"id":"bts7960","name":"Big motor driver (BTS7960, 43 A)","description":"One big DC motor (a car seat motor, a wheelchair motor) from B+ / B- (6-27 V, up to 43 A). RPWM drives it one way, LPWM the other (analogWrite on one, the other LOW); R_EN and L_EN must both be HIGH. VCC is the logic supply (5 V).","swatch":"#2a2c31","mass":66,"shape":[{"box":[5,0.16,5],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#b0302a"},{"box":[4,4.14,3],"at":[0,2.23,0.4],"color":"#9aa0aa"},{"box":[1.6,1,0.9],"at":[-1.1,0.66,-2.2],"color":"#2a62c8"},{"box":[1.6,1,0.9],"at":[1.1,0.66,-2.2],"color":"#2a62c8"}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["RPWM","LPWM","R_EN","L_EN","R_IS","L_IS","VCC","GND"],"at":[-0.889,0.16,2.3],"dir":"x","kinds":{"RPWM":"in","LPWM":"in","R_EN":"in","L_EN":"in","R_IS":"out","L_IS":"out","VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (logic 5 V)","vmin":3.3,"vmax":5.5}}}],"pins":[{"id":"B+","label":"B+ (6-27 V)","at":[-1.5,1.16,-2.4],"kind":"vin","vmin":5.5,"vmax":27},{"id":"B-","at":[-0.7,1.16,-2.4],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"M+","label":"Motor +","at":[0.7,1.16,-2.4],"kind":"motor"},{"id":"M-","label":"Motor -","at":[1.5,1.16,-2.4],"kind":"motor"}],"device":"bts7960"},{"id":"vibration-motor","name":"Vibration motor (eccentric weight)","description":"A little motor with an off-centre weight on its shaft (as in a phone or a game pad): powered (about 3 V, 80 mA) it spins at about 10 000 rpm and shakes whatever it's glued to. Small ones are fine on a pin through a transistor; straight on a pin is too much current.","swatch":"#b9bec7","mass":4,"shape":[{"cyl":[0.35,1.2],"at":[0,0.35,0],"rot":[0,0,90],"color":"#b9bec7"}],"pins":[{"id":"+","label":"+ (red)","at":[-0.7,0.35,0.15],"kind":"motor"},{"id":"-","label":"- (black)","at":[-0.7,0.35,-0.15],"kind":"motor"}],"moving":[{"id":"weight","mass":0.5,"shape":[{"box":[0.25,0.5,0.3],"at":[0.75,0.6,0],"color":"#d9d9d9"}],"joint":{"type":"turn","at":[0.75,0.35,0],"axis":[1,0,0],"motor":"motor","torque":0.02,"speed":10000,"volts":3}}],"device":"vibration"},{"id":"solenoid","name":"Push-pull solenoid (12 V)","description":"An electromagnet pulling a steel plunger in when powered (12 V, about 0.6 A, 5 N pull over 1 cm); a spring pushes it back out when it's off. Switch it with a transistor, a MOSFET or a relay, never straight from a pin.","swatch":"#9aa0aa","mass":25,"shape":[{"box":[1.5,1.3,3],"at":[0,0.65,0],"color":"#9aa0aa"},{"cyl":[0.6,2.8],"at":[0,0.65,0],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#c8873a","collide":false}],"pins":[{"id":"+","label":"+ (12 V)","at":[-0.3,1.3,-1.6],"kind":"motor"},{"id":"-","at":[0.3,1.3,-1.6],"kind":"motor"}],"moving":[{"id":"plunger","mass":6,"shape":[{"cyl":[0.3,3],"at":[0,0.65,2],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#c7c9cc"},{"cyl":[0.4,0.2],"at":[0,0.65,3.5],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#c7c9cc"}],"joint":{"type":"slide","at":[0,0.65,1.5],"axis":[0,0,1],"motor":"servo","force":5,"speed":60,"volts":12,"min":-1,"max":0}}],"device":"solenoid"},{"id":"linear-actuator","name":"Linear actuator (12 V, 10 cm)","description":"A motor turning a screw that pushes a rod out or pulls it in: about 1.5 cm/s and 200 N at 12 V, 10 cm of travel, with switches inside that stop it at each end. Wire M+ / M- like a DC motor (through a motor driver or a relay pair): reversing the voltage reverses it.","swatch":"#4a4f57","mass":450,"shape":[{"box":[3,3,16.5],"at":[0,1.5,-0.25],"color":"#4a4f57"},{"box":[3.4,3.4,4.5],"at":[0,1.7,-6.9],"color":"#2a2c31"}],"pins":[{"id":"M+","label":"Motor +","at":[-0.6,3.4,-9.2],"kind":"motor"},{"id":"M-","label":"Motor -","at":[0.6,3.4,-9.2],"kind":"motor"}],"moving":[{"id":"rod","mass":60,"shape":[{"cyl":[0.5,12],"at":[0,1.5,4.35],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#c7c9cc"},{"box":[1.4,1.4,1],"at":[0,1.5,10.85],"color":"#9aa0aa"}],"joint":{"type":"slide","at":[0,1.5,8],"axis":[0,0,1],"motor":"motor","force":200,"speed":1.5,"volts":12,"min":0,"max":10}}],"device":"actuator"}]}